      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4710",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/assets/afe1d7178e71e62c839c286ed0b30d95d53546f03242839814d7a737c65c134f.png)\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/assets/5a1ea521da77b55ba6e85a5ca964ddfbb7d53dd44e4aa5a3317b33b04fedd401.png)\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=3,$ $y=-2,$ and $z=0.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle 3,-2,0 \\rangle.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
